.TH BYTE_SKIP 3
.SH NAME
byte_skip \- count the run of a byte at the start of a byte array
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <byte.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t byte_skip(const void* " p ", size_t " n ", char " c ");
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B byte_skip
returns the number of consecutive bytes equal to c at the start of p.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The run length; if the whole array is c, or n is 0, it returns n.
.PP
These are the single-byte counterparts of the scan_charset*skip functions.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR byte_rskip (3),
.BR byte_skipn (3)
